# Frontend local rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/engineering/frontend.md` first.
- Templates render server-provided data; JavaScript owns interaction, not
  permissions, workflow truth, authoritative filtering, or state transitions.
- Reuse shared fetch/error, CSRF, toast, modal, pagination, dropdown, form, and
  loading/empty/error-state behavior before adding a page-local copy.
- Extract shared code only when the repeated behavior is stable and genuinely
  identical; do not build speculative component frameworks.
- Keep common CSS tokens/components separate from page CSS. Keep each page
  script capability-focused and within the repository file-size gate.
- Open internal links in the current page by default. New-window behavior needs
  an explicit requirement and `noopener` protection.
- UI work is not verified until authenticated browser interaction, visual state,
  Console/network results, and loaded assets are checked.

## Theme

- Theme follows frontend.md Theme Contract
- page CSS must use semantic tokens
- no page-local dark system
- materially modified UI must be checked in light and dark
- hardcoded theme colors require justification
